        "title": "Fuel-Pump Wiring Can Short, Disable the Vehicle, or Cause a Fire (Recall)",
        "description": "NHTSA campaign 99V028000 covers certain 1994-1995 Ford Aerostar minivans. Heat in the wiring harness to the fuel-pump and sender assembly can create an electrical short. An affected vehicle may lose power and become immobilized, the fuel gauge may behave erratically, and heat damage can melt or char the harness; the short can also cause a vehicle fire.",
        "solution": "Check the VIN for an open recall with NHTSA or a Ford dealer. The recall remedy is installation of a fused jumper harness in the fuel-pump ground circuit at the fuel-pump inertia shut-off switch. Do not replace the pump or relay solely from the former generic card.",
