        "title": "AWD Transfer-Case or Transmission Structure Can Fail (Recalls)",
        "description": "NHTSA campaigns 97V204000 and 99V094000 cover affected 1992-1997 all-wheel-drive Ford Aerostar minivans, with the later campaign adding 1992 vehicles not included previously. Powertrain bending resonance or displacement of the transfer-case output-shaft bushing can cause structural failure of the transmission and/or transfer case. Fluid expulsion, driveshaft separation, or loss of drive can result, creating loss-of-control and fire risks.",
        "solution": "Check the VIN for both campaigns with NHTSA or a Ford dealer. The recall remedy is installation of a new transfer-case rear output-shaft bushing and an aluminum driveshaft. The former A4LD rebuild, shift-kit, fluid-interval, and transmission-swap advice is not part of these campaigns.",
